            "review_text": "Joshua R\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam31 contributions\n0\nOne of the best meals I've had inside a mall.\nMay 2018\nI was told by a friend this is a Hong Kong style restaurant with some dim sum dishes and milk tea on the menu. We ordered some dim sum which was tasty, but a little unusual. We preferred plain steamed rice, the duck which had crispy skin and was tender and juicy. The roasted pork belly was also well cooked and served with a spicy mustard sauce which I found delicious. Vegetables were delicious, not overcooked and had just enough oyster sauce to flavor them without drowning them in the seasoning. Service was quick and efficient.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 30, 2018",
